# Photograph the sneak-attack gate for a rogue's FIRST blow from Improved
# Invisibility at range, against a victim that has Blind-Fight. Part of bead
# inc-nkf2.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-sneak-invis-maxhp.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/orc-rogue-sneak-seed1.sav \
#   INCURSION_SNEAK_PROBE=1 \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/sneak-invis-ranged.keys <seed>
#
# Read the result with tools/check_sneak_invis.sh.
#
# THE VICTIM has FT_BLIND_FIGHT. lib/mon2.irh:2004 green hag carries it
# (Feats: ..., FT_BLIND_FIGHT, ...), is SZ_MEDIUM, living and crit-vulnerable,
# and has no M_SEE_INVIS. It does have CA_INFRAVISION, which is why this run
# needs no light spell: in the unlit arrival room the hag perceives the rogue
# while the rogue is visible (Perceives()'s infravision branch), and
# invisibility skips that branch too (the INVIS test at src/Vision.cpp:907
# jumps over the infravision block).
#
# THE ATTACK IS THROWN, so it is RANGED. The rogue's orcish knife is
# IT_THROWABLE; the game's own ranged weapon menu (src/Player.cpp:711 "Throw
# what?") offers it. The green hag is summoned two squares east, so the
# throw resolves at distance 2 -- inside the game's ranged band, and squarely
# the case the brief asks for.
#
# WHY NO CONTROL. The question here is narrow: with Blind-Fight the victim's
# surprise flag is set by the "!Perceives && !HasFeat(FT_BLIND_FIGHT)" test at
# src/Fight.cpp:4152, which Blind-Fight disables entirely. The probe's "pre"
# line records isSurprise before the Move Silently vs Listen contest and before
# damage, so the surprise count is read straight off it. Whether the blow then
# lands and reaches the sneak gate is counted separately, the same way case A
# is.
#
# The victim is freshly summoned, so it is flat-footed and the sneak gate can
# open on flatfoot=1 alone even with surprise=0. That is why this case counts
# surprise and sneak separately rather than claiming sneak proves anything on
# its own. Measured: the first ranged blow reads surprise=0 with FT_BLIND_FIGHT
# (unchallenged, since the victim's feat suppresses the unseen-surprise branch
# outright), while a landed blow is awarded sneak dice through flatfoot=1, not
# through invisibility.

# The rogue is LOADED (INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/orc-rogue-sneak-seed1.sav,
# made by tools/keys/sneak-invis-rogue-save.keys); there is no chargen here.
@dump:arrival
i       # inventory: the starting kit leaves the knife in the pack, and the
0 1     # throw menu offers only what is wielded or on the belt, so take
SPACE   # the knife (pack item 01) out, put it on the weapon hand (b), and
b       # answer the swap prompts
SPACE
n
ESC

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
SPACE   # Cheat Death
DOWN*7
SPACE   # Infinite Mana
ESC

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Improved Invisibility" ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"True Seeing" ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC

# True Seeing on the rogue: the green hag casts Invisibility on herself at
# creation, and an attacker who cannot see its victim suffers a 50% wild miss
# (src/Fight.cpp, vicUnseen) that no switch controls. True Seeing removes it.
m
@cursorto:mark "True Seeing" DOWN
ENTER
*
@while "Take opportunity" y
@while "Die?" n
@dump:trueseeing

# Summon the green hag one square east (a freshly summoned creature is
# flat-footed).
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Hags"
@choose "green hag"
RIGHT ENTER
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:victim

# SETUP: a visible melee blow at the hag. It zeroes both fighters' FFCount
# (src/Fight.cpp Creature::Hit), so the measured throw below hits a hag that is
# no longer flat-footed. The probe reads invisVal=-1 flatfoot=1 for it, so the
# check does not count it as a case C blow. The hag may have cast Invisibility
# on itself, so the walk can meet either prompt.
RIGHT
@while "Confirm attack" y
@while "Attack?" y
@while "Take opportunity" y
@while "Die?" n
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:setup

# Cast Improved Invisibility, so the throw below is the first blow after it.
m
@cursorto:mark "Improved Invisibility" DOWN
ENTER
*
@while "Take opportunity" y
@while "Die?" n
@dump:cast

# Step one square west: the hag is now two squares east, inside the ranged band.
LEFT
@while "Take opportunity" y
@while "Die?" n
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:stepped

# The measured blow: throw the knife at the hag, two squares east. The target
# cursor starts on the rogue's own square.
f
@choose "orcish knife"
RIGHT*2 ENTER
@while "Take opportunity" y
@while "Die?" n
@until "HP:" ESC
@dump:thrown

@quit
